===== commit messages for the recent seed work (#192,#193) =====
6e0fcf1 feat(seed): swap faker.lorem bodies for an original literary-fixture pool (#193)
Adds backend/scripts/dev-prose-pool.ts — a pool of 22 original
literary-erotica fixture pieces (~23k words total, lengths 555-1620
each) generated for the project and owned by the project. The seed
script now draws bodies from this pool instead of faker.lorem, so the
fixture rows on the dev server read as coherent literary prose rather
than nonsense paragraphs.

backend/scripts/dev-prose-pool.ts (new, 1440 lines)
- Six writer agents produced 22 pieces across distinct registers
  (first-person past, first-person present, third-person close,
  epistolary, prose-poetry, kink-aware literary) so the pool isn't
  uniform.
- Each piece exports { title, excerpt, body, wordCount, suggestedTags,
  notes } via a `DevProsePiece` type.
- Plain TypeScript constant — imported only by the dev seeder, never
  bundled into anything shipped.

backend/scripts/seed-dev-content.ts — three surgical changes:
1. Two new constants:
   - POOL_IDENTITY_REUSE_RATIO (0.4) — fraction of seeded rows that
     reuse a pool piece's title + excerpt verbatim (the rest stay on
     the faker-driven generators so the pool isn't visibly over-used).
   - POOL_VERBATIM_TOLERANCE (0.35) — body is used verbatim when the
     wordTarget is within +/- this fraction of the piece's wordCount.
2. Three new helpers: pickPoolPiece (uniform), pickPoolPieceForWordTarget
   (length-filtered with uniform fallback), derivedTagsFromPiece
   (case-insensitive substring match in both directions against the
   real tag taxonomy, then fills remaining slots via the existing
   pickTags so the adult/safe ratio is honored). generateBody is
   rewritten to use a primary pool piece verbatim when length matches,
   else concatenate up to 3 distinct pieces with a `---` section break.
3. planStory and planSeries anchor each row to a single pool piece —
   the piece's body, derived tags, and probabilistically its title +
   excerpt all derive from it, so a returning reader sees a coherent
   fixture instead of mismatched pieces.

Header comment updated to reflect the new content sources.

All four safety guards (LUCIFER_ENV, DATABASE_URL prod sniff,

===== seed-dev-content.ts : header / guards / how-to-run =====
/* eslint-disable no-console */
// =====================================================================
// seed-dev-content — DEV-ONLY synthetic content seeder.
//
// Generates 50 published + 5 draft standalone stories and 8 published
// + 1 fully-draft series (3-8 chapters each) so the GSAP work shipped
// in PRs #187-#191 (scroll restore / button feedback / Flip note
// expand / magnetic dock / Flip tag filter) has something real to
// animate against in dev.
//
// CONTENT SOURCES:
//   - Bodies (and ~40% of titles + excerpts): drawn from the original
//     project-owned literary fixture pool in ./dev-prose-pool.ts —
//     22 pieces generated for this project, no external source.
//   - The remaining ~60% of titles + excerpts: hand-curated mood-noun
//     pool + faker words, kept so the pool isn't visibly over-repeated
//     on a single seed run.
//   - When the chosen wordTarget for a row falls outside any single
//     pool piece's wordCount tolerance, the body is built by joining
//     2-3 pool pieces with a "---" section break. Pure faker.lorem
//     remains in the file as a defensive fallback but isn't exercised
//     by the current call sites.
//
// SAFETY (three independent guards; all must pass):
//   1. process.env.LUCIFER_ENV must equal "dev". Refuses otherwise.
//   2. process.env.DATABASE_URL is scanned for production markers
//      (prod, production, render.com, neon.tech, supabase.co,
//      rds.amazonaws.com). Match → refuse.
//   3. --confirm=dev is required on every command that writes
//      (seed + purge). Only --dry-run is exempt.
//
// IDEMPOTENT: every seeded row is tagged with the SEED_MARKER token
// hidden in its authorsNote field. The script refuses to seed if any
// marker rows already exist; --purge wipes ONLY marker rows.
//
// COMMANDS:
//   LUCIFER_ENV=dev npm run seed:dev -- --confirm=dev   populate
//   LUCIFER_ENV=dev npm run seed:dev -- --dry-run       preview, zero writes
//   LUCIFER_ENV=dev npm run seed:dev -- --purge --confirm=dev   wipe seeded rows
// =====================================================================

import { PrismaClient, type Tag } from '@prisma/client';
import { faker } from '@faker-js/faker';
import { DEV_PROSE_POOL, type DevProsePiece } from './dev-prose-pool';

// ── Constants ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/**
 * Hidden authorsNote sentinel. Invisible to readers (only surfaces in
 * the admin UI), screenshot-safe, and the matcher for --purge. Every
 * seeded row's authorsNote STARTS WITH this string — purge filters
 * accordingly.
 */
const SEED_MARKER = '[dev-seed-fixture]';

const PUBLISHED_STORY_COUNT = 50;
const DRAFT_STORY_COUNT = 5;
const PUBLISHED_SERIES_COUNT = 8;
const DRAFT_SERIES_COUNT = 1;
const CHAPTERS_PER_SERIES_MIN = 3;

